iteria":["G6"],"decision":"block","decision_margin":0.2,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Plan: 'sandbox-exec is Apple-deprecated, so its enforcement is a load-bearing external capability ... Deprecation is a future risk, not a current gap — the fail-closed posture turns a breakage into an abort.'","scripts/mutation_sandbox.py:75 `if shutil.which(\"sandbox-exec\"): return SEATBELT` — presence-only, no functional probe","Contrast scripts/mutation_sandbox.py:77 bwrap: `if shutil.which(\"bwrap\") and _bwrap_works()` — functionally probed","Plan's own disqualifier: bwrap AC notes 'Presence is not capability ... a PATH-only probe reports available then fails to enforce — the flaw that disqualified unshare' — the same reasoning is not applied to Seatbelt"],"finding":"The plan claims the macOS fail-closed posture 'turns a breakage into an abort', but the sandbox mechanism only detects sandbox-exec by PATH presence, not functional enforcement — a present-but-non-enforcing (deprecated/no-op) sandbox-exec would proceed effectively unsandboxed rather than abort, contradicting the fail-closed claim and applying a weaker probe to Seatbelt than to bwrap.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f6a16b0c0f5391a9b","impact":1.0,"is_primary":null,"location":"Mechanisms — 'macOS — Seatbelt' paragraph; AC 'macOS uses Seatbelt sandbox-exec with a generated profile'","norm_id":"n74179ec4fa0a6554","priority":1.0,"reason":"high-priority+criterion-opted-in","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A future macOS where sandbox-exec is present but its enforcement was removed/neutered: probe() returns SEATBELT, the profile is written, the child runs, and a destructive mutant is NOT contained — yet no abort fires."],"severity":"critical","suggested_fix":"Add a `_seatbelt_works()` functional probe mirroring `_bwrap_works()` — run `sandbox-exec` with a deny-file-write profile over a scratch write and require the write to fail — and gate the SEATBELT branch of `probe()` on it, so a non-enforcing sandbox-exec falls through to the abort/opt-out path.","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"yes","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"yes","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"no","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"contradicts_reality","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"medium","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"medium","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"silent","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":null,"blocking_enabled":null,"checklist_item":"","cohort":null,"criteria":["P6"],"decision":"advisory","decision_margin":null,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["1 criterion line(s) bundle multiple deliverables with 'and' (split so each is independently verifiable)."],"finding":"Acceptance-criteria / definition-of-done quality issues.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f607dd457c67f9209","impact":0.4,"is_primary":null,"location":"","norm_id":"ned06ebc801a522e3","priority":0.4,"reason":null,"recalled":false,"scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Split compound criteria, replace subjective terms with observable outcomes, and state how each is verified.","tier":"DET","validity":1.0,"verification":null},{"block_threshold":0.8,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Enumerate the allow-list's writable members in AC1 (e.g. the git-archive temp source tree and mutmut's working/cache dir), not only the venv exclusion, so the executor need not infer them.","cohort":["COH","E1","E2","E6","F1","T2","T4","T5e"],"criteria":["E2"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.767,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["\"denying writes outside an explicit allow-list\"","\"The venv is deliberately EXCLUDED from it\"","AC exclusions are stated (venv) but inclusions are not — implicit acceptance criteria under E2 signal (2)"],"finding":"AC1 requires writes denied 'outside an explicit allow-list' and excludes the venv, but the plan never enumerates what the allow-list DOES contain — the executor must infer which paths (git-archive temp source tree, a build/tmp dir mutmut writes to, cache dirs) are writable for the sandboxed pytest/mutmut run to function at all.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"fbb8976279cef8f76","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance Criteria, AC1","norm_id":"n1d3ec842be2b4b5a","priority":0.033,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Executor wraps mutmut run in a sandbox that denies writes to the temp source tree, and pytest/mutmut can no longer write its own artifacts, breaking the run for a reason unrelated to a mutant."],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"State the default: allow writes only to the git-archive temp source tree (and any tmp/cache dir mutmut requires), deny everything else including the venv and $HOME.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.125,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"no","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"low","